    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Ennis Gough Property is delighted to offer home buyers the opportunity to look at this lovely terraced house in the popular Abbey Park, Ferrybank. \r\nThis lovely home is located at the rear of the development therefore there is very little passing traffic. The property is a two storey terraced dwelling with a separate garage, and easy access at the back into the rear garden.  \r\nThe original dining room of this house has been repurposed as a downstairs bedroom with en-suite WC.  This arrangement can be easily reversed if not needed. Central heating is with a solid fuel back boiler. This can be upgraded to gas as a supply is already available off the gas mains on the road outside. \r\nThe property overlooks an expansive shared green area. The surroundings are quiet, yet there is a regular bus to the city centre and a late night supermarket (Tesco) close to hand.  Ferrybank's three schools are walking distance, and the nearby Ross Abbey Centre provides a selection of amenities including coffee shop, Tesco, Mr Price, takeaway, fitness, beauty, barbers and dog grooming, among others.  Aldi, Ferrybank library, and the new health centre are a short drive away. \r\nFerrybank's new Greenway, linking Waterford and New Ross is due to open early next year with access off the Abbey Road, near the Abbey Church.\r\nCommuters will appreciate the speedy access to the N24/ N25 and M9, which provide links to other towns and cities in all directions.\r\nThis property is presented in excellent decorative condition and ready for its new owners to move in and unpack. \r\nThere is no vendor chain in this sale.  There are no RPZ restrictions on this property."
      },
      {
